# =============================================================================
# ClinIQ — environment settings TEMPLATE
# =============================================================================
# HOW TO USE THIS FILE
#   1. Copy it to a new file called ".env" in this same folder (icu_monitor/):
#          cp .env.example .env
#      (python setup.py does this for you if .env does not exist yet.)
#   2. Open .env and replace the placeholder below with your real key.
#   3. Restart the backend so it reads the new value:
#          uvicorn backend.main:app --reload --port 8000
#
# SAFETY RULES
#   - This file (.env.example) is a template. It is safe to commit because it
#     holds only a placeholder, never a real key.
#   - ".env" holds the REAL key. It is listed in .gitignore and must NEVER be
#     committed, pasted into a chat, or sent to anyone.
#   - Write each setting on one line as NAME=value: no spaces around "=",
#     no quotes around the value.
#
# This is the ONLY setting the project reads from the environment
# (backend/api/report.py reads it; backend/main.py loads this file at start-up).
# =============================================================================

# Groq API key — REQUIRED for the AI Clinical Report.
#   What it is used for : writing each clinical report and judging its reliability
#                         (model openai/gpt-oss-120b on Groq).
#   Without it          : the vitals, SOFA score, alert, trends and SHAP
#                         explanations all still work. Only POST /api/report
#                         fails, with the error "GROQ_API_KEY not configured".
#   Where to get one    : free at https://console.groq.com  (API Keys → Create)
#   What it looks like  : starts with "gsk_" followed by about 52 characters.
GROQ_API_KEY=your_groq_api_key_here
